  "final_message": "I have started listing the files in the workspace and will inspect the codebase once complete.\nI am running the test suite to establish the baseline before making any changes.\nI am compiling the code and executing the tests with the updated `OrderPlaced` event structure.\nI will wait for the test run to finish.\nI will wait for the architecture rule checks to complete.\nI will wait for git diff to return.\nThe [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L36) event has been updated to align field naming with the Payments and Customer APIs while complying with architecture rule **ARCH-4** (*\"OrderPlaced and OrderCancelled are consumed by services in other repositories: billing-service and analytics-ingest. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation\"*).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **[`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts)**:\n   - Added `amountCents` (integer, minor units) and `createdAt` (ISO-8601 instant) to the [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L36) interface.\n   - Preserved `totalCents` and `placedAt` as `@deprecated` fields so existing deployed consumers in `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` remain unbroken.\n   - Updated [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L52-L72) to populate both the new fields (`amountCents`, `createdAt`) and the deprecated legacy fields (`totalCents`, `placedAt`).\n\n2. **Tests ([`test/app.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/test/app.test.ts), [`test/adapters.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/test/adapters.test.ts))**:\n   - Added assertions to verify `amountCents` and `createdAt` are emitted in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L36) events alongside `totalCents` and `placedAt`.\n\n### Verification\n\nAll checks have succeeded:\n- `npm run build` compiled without errors.\n- `npm test` passed (39/39 tests passing).\n- `npm run typecheck` verified types without errors.\n- `npm run arch` passed dependency-cruiser checks with 0 violations.\n",
